                <pb facs="0133" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg49"/>

                <head>No. 36.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pringle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 18,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 305.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received Mr. Hall’s confidential
                    dispatch No. 404, of August 31 last, announcing that ex-President Zavala, of
                    Nicaragua, had accomplished the object of his recent visit to Guatemala, and
                    that the amicable relations between those two sister Republics, which the decree
                    of the late President Barrios, of February 28 last, had temporarily interrupted,
                    had been re-established.</p>
                <p>The President directs me to say that he has been much gratified at this
                    intelligence, and to express his willingness to permit our representatives in
                    Central America to use their influence to that end when it can be done with full
                    recognition of the sovereign rights of those states. He hopes, also, as do the
                    people of the United States, that not only may there be between the Central
                    American Republics the most perfect, cordial, and friendly understanding, but
                    that the fullest measure of success may be realized through their combined
                    peaceful endeavors, and a new era of prosperity be vouchsafed unto them.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
